wip/ovito: Import ovito-3.17.1

OVITO (Open Visualization Tool) visualizes and analyses atomistic,
molecular and other particle-based simulation data.  This is the
open-source code base of OVITO Basic, built from the 3.17.1 release
commit on gitlab.com/stuko/ovito (the release is not tagged there).

Builds the Qt6 desktop application with all open-source plugins and
the real-time "standard" renderer (Qt RHI; Metal on macOS, Vulkan
elsewhere), which replaced the OpenGL renderer in 3.16.  FFmpeg video
output (ffmpeg7), NetCDF/HDF5, SQLite and the libssh client come from
pkgsrc; zstd 1.5.7 is built from the bundled sources as upstream
requires (its zlib wrapper is not installed by archivers/zstd).

The Python module (PyScript) and the Tachyon, OSPRay, VisRTX and ANARI
renderers are proprietary OVITO Pro components and are not in the
source repository.

On Darwin the GUI is installed as ${PREFIX}/Applications/Ovito.app with
a launcher in bin; the bundle fixup that copies Qt into the bundle is
skipped, and the @rpath install names are made absolute after install.
